WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.425
Secondary Memory

00:00:02.775 --> 00:00:06.200
The primary memory is limited and temporary.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:11.608
Therefore, there is a need for secondary memory that can be used to store large

00:00:11.608 --> 00:00:13.400
amounts of data permanently.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.550
The data remains there even when the power to the computer is switched off.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.575
Some commonly used secondary storage device are as follows

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:26.525
Hard Disk

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:28.575
Compact Disc

00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:31.750
DVD (Digital Versatile Disk)

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.700
Pen drive

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.750
Memory Card

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.200
Hard Disk

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.500
A hard disk is the main secondary storage device.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.200
A hard disk is a device fixed inside the CPU box.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.275
It can store a huge amount of data.

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:57.075
All the work done on a computer can be stored on a hard disk.

00:00:57.425 --> 00:01:01.825
We can read and write data on this device any number of times.

00:01:03.675 --> 00:01:05.550
TYPES OF HARD DISKS

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.525
Let us see different types of hard disks.

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.300
INTERNAL HARD DISK

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:18.231
The internal hard disk is the main secondary storage device that is permanently

00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:20.350
installed inside the computer.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.687
It can store a huge amount of data that includes the operating system,

00:01:25.687 --> 00:01:29.533
application programs and other data, including images,

00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:32.525
documents, music and videos on a computer.

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:36.827
The hard disk is usually given a label such as C:

00:01:36.827 --> 00:01:39.650
or D: called as C drive or D drive.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.375
EXTERNAL HARD DISK

00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:49.875
An external hard disk is a removable hard disk that connects to a computer through a

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:50.900
USB connector.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.893
You can plug in an external hard disk into multiple computers and use it as a

00:01:56.893 --> 00:01:58.725
removable storage device.

00:01:59.075 --> 00:02:04.250
An external hard disk is, however, slower than an internal hard disk.
